BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Bird Walk
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTSTAMP:20261120T185733Z
UID:f9396f3b2dc077d11e5a0f1e45a1@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:One of the best spots in Connecticut look for birds is Hammona
 sset State Park. It's mix of habitats attracts more species than any other
  park in the state. We'll search for late fall migrants and early winter r
 esidents in the salt marshes\, open fields\, and along the coast. Walk wil
 l be approximately 1-1.25 miles on level dirt\, grass\, and sandy terrain.
  Exposure to cold\, wind\, and sun possible depending on weather. Portable
  toilets on site.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/fall-bird-walk-15
LOCATION:Hammonasset State Park\, 1288 Boston Post Rd\, Madison CT\, 06443
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/fall-bird-walk-15
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Planting for Birds – Winter Session
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTSTAMP:20261120T185733Z
UID:03c193fbd2eca6fb1a301088b54c@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:While habitat loss poses challenges for birds and wildlife wor
 ldwide\, creating backyard habitats offers a solution! In this four-part s
 eries\, participants will learn about ways to improve backyard habitats th
 roughout different seasons. Each program will focus on the seasonal needs 
 of birds and specific ways to support them\, using examples from the sanct
 uary grounds of the RTP Estuary Center in Old Lyme. Each session will incl
 ude an indoor presentation and an outdoor exploration of the sanctuary gro
 unds and gardens\, accompanied by handouts that list the plants mentioned 
 for each session.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/planting-birds-win
 ter-session
LOCATION:RTP Estuary Center\, 100 Lyme Street\, Old Lyme CT\, 06371
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/planting-birds-winter-session
END:VEVENT
